+## Independent review
+
+Review depth follows the claim's consequence and uncertainty, recorded in the existing brief/result/review. Early feasibility and pilot work needs targeted source and correctness checks. A source-only closure without a main claim, or a demonstrably immaterial recipe, may end in a brief checked closeout without exhaustive independent numerical reconstruction. State what was checked; unreviewed or unresolved results remain provisional and scoped.
+
+Before accepting a consequential finding or materially funding its confirmation, a fresh Sol/max reviewer distinct from the author first assesses scientific payoff, closest prior, strongest surviving alternative and information/design adequacy, including relevant input privileges, comparators, endpoints and independent units. Then choose the necessary independent reconstruction and highest-value falsification. Inspect actual relevant outputs; use an independent method where shared implementation could hide a decisive error. Do not rerun every auxiliary calculation by default. A distinct implementation using common sources/reference data is not independent biological replication. Neither code nor agent agreement establishes importance or truth.
+
+When review identifies a useful discriminating test, the PI may revise within the brief's explicitly developmental scope and remaining resources; outside that scope requires a revised investment decision. Preserve original frozen tests, gates, failures and all exposure. Label new tests developmental/postvalidation as appropriate, freeze consequential choices before new evaluation and obtain genuinely independent evidence where the claim requires it. Never retune consumed validation into a new primary success.
+
+A newly found numerical bug requires tracing affected outputs/claims, preserving failed versions and the amendment, and correcting/rechecking those dependencies; extend reruns only where the impact warrants. Narrow, bank, revise or close with uncertainties explicit. Further review needs material unresolved doubt or new evidence, not universal one-contrary, one-revision or every-pair quotas, or an infinite review-of-review chain. Use existing roles and artifacts.
+
